  // ─── [/VERIFY] ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  // ─── [DAMAGE] ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What the edits BROKE, as opposed to whether they did what was asked.
  //
  // Every existing pass judges the edits against the REQUEST. The coverage
  // audit scores a checklist derived from what you wanted, so an edit that
  // satisfies the request while damaging the clause around it scores
  // clean — nothing is looking for damage, because nobody asked for any.
  //
  // Seen in the wild: language added to a long clause that already stated
  // its purpose, leaving the purpose stated twice. No requirement covered
  // it, the deterministic checks do not model meaning, and the coverage
  // audit read past it because the requirement it was scoring was met.
  //
  // WHY A MODEL AND NOT A DETERMINISTIC CHECK. The rest of [VERIFY] is
  // deterministic because term extraction is mechanical: a term is defined
  // or it is not. This is not. The duplication a model produces is almost
  // never verbatim — it re-expresses the thought in different words, which
  // is invisible to any lexical measure and obvious to a reader. So this
  // asks a reader.
  //
  // It costs ONE call. The question is asked once, over the FINAL edit set
  // — after the coverage loop has added its own edits, so it judges the
  // document everything else has finished with.
  // TO REMOVE: delete to [/DAMAGE] + its call in _runChain +
  // _renderDamageSection's line in _bodyReview.

  function _buildDamagePrompt(active, payload, touched) {
    return [
      "You are a senior associate proof-reading " + _dkNounA() + " that has just been",
      "amended. You did not make the amendments and you are not judging them.",
      "",
      "ONE QUESTION: reading the document below as it now stands, is there",
      "anything WRONG WITH IT that was not wrong before?",
      "",
      "Look hardest at the amended paragraphs and the ones around them:",
      "- the same point now made TWICE — a purpose, an obligation, a carve-out",
      "  or a definition stated once in the original wording and again in the",
      "  new. It will usually be in DIFFERENT words, not a copy.",
      "- new language that CONTRADICTS a part of the document nobody touched",
      "- a sentence that no longer follows from the one before it, or a",
      "  connector left dangling — \"such\", \"the foregoing\", \"in addition\"",
      "  pointing at something that is no longer there",
      "- a defined term used in a sense the definition does not carry, or a",
      "  capitalised term that reads as defined and is not",
      "- numbering, lettering or a cross-reference that no longer lines up",
      "- a register that jumps: plain drafting dropped into a formal clause",
      "  or the reverse",
      "",
      "RULES:",
      "1. Only what is WRONG. Not what you would have drafted differently —",
      "   a proof-reader who lists preferences is ignored, and then the real",
      "   findings are ignored with them.",
      "2. Do NOT report anything MISSING. Another pass owns that, and it has",
      "   the client's request; you do not.",
      "3. Quote the text that shows it. A finding with no quote is not one.",
      "4. If the document reads correctly, return an empty list. That is a",
      "   normal answer and the expected one.",
      "",
      "Return JSON only:",
      "{",
      '  "problems": [',
      '    { "where": "Section 4.2", "what": "<one sentence: what is wrong>",',
      '      "quote": "<the words that show it>",',
      '      "alsoAt": "<the other place, when the problem is a repeat — else \\"\\">",',
      '      "severity": "high|medium|low" }',
      "  ]",
      "}",
      "",
      "═══ THE PARAGRAPHS THAT WERE AMENDED ═══",
      touched.length ? touched.join(", ") : "(none recorded — read it all)",
      "",
      "═══ THE DOCUMENT AS IT NOW READS (paragraph-indexed) ═══",
      JSON.stringify(payload, null, 1),
